From fbb6d0d2c700f99ec2c4c066d4e1479dd5b2178f Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Hades <15710513+hadesdevls@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Sun, 27 Sep 2026 22:08:59 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] dvbridge: bounded diagnostics of Dolby Vision output failures

A frame that cannot be shown left no trace: on real NVIDIA hardware the
picture froze while audio went on, and the log did not say at which step
the native Dolby Vision path failed.

Adapted from CroqueMr/intel-dv-libreelec commit
73d61bf60e7d848efcc6d3653e6ac9e84acdbc38, patches/kodi/kodi-9991-diagnostics.patch
(GPL-2.0-or-later): rate-limited reports of the failing stage in the GL
bridge (initialization, layer import, reconstruction, packing) and in the
atomic commit (property assembly, TEST_ONLY, commit, framebuffer), with
the first failure always reported and later ones at most every five
seconds; debug-level logs of stream selection, captured properties and
output transitions. Its DRMAtomic.h hunks are applied by hand on top of
the output selection change.

Hades additions, through the same rate limiter:
- the VAAPI renderer reports why a Dolby Vision frame is not handed to
  the bridge (texture target, orientation, surface format, cropping,
  missing metadata), which was silent;
- BeginDVBridge reports which precondition refused native output (mode,
  bit depth, GLES 3, bridge initialization, property capture, GUI
  compositing), which was silent;
- the first rejected commit is logged with its properties even without
  debug logging.

Diagnostics only: no decision about what is presented changes.
